Aerie-Purpose: Let Ctrl+W on a Pinned or Favorites tab follow the pinned-close setting instead of closing the tab.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui (browser_commands.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #180. chrome::CloseTab runs for IDC_CLOSE_TAB (Ctrl+W, Cmd+W). Before it closes the selected tab it
calls aerie_tab_model::HandlePinnedClose (overlay, chrome/browser/aerie_tab_model/pinned_close_hook.h). For a
tab of Aerie's Pinned section or Favorites grid that call applies the aerie.tabs.pinned_close setting (reset,
sleep and switch; sleep only; or close) and returns true, and CloseTab returns. For any other tab it returns
false and nothing changes. Chromium's own "close pinned tab" toast is for tabs that carry the Chromium pinned
bit, which Aerie's Pinned tabs do not (docs/sidebar-design.md, "Pinned tabs and the Chromium pinned bit").
The header has no dependencies, so the new dep of browser_commands_impl cannot make a cycle; the definition is
in pinned_tabs_controller.cc.

